s or  perhaps another example of empty virtue  signaling  than if you i think it's both i think it  is empty virtue signaling because it  just reveals that there's nothing we can  do but on the other hand i know that a  lot of people in ukraine feel genuinely  grateful for the practical support that  britain in particular has given but also  for the moral support so i i haven't put  any flags in my social media handles or  whatever because i just think  i've never been a fan of doing that  but i know that there will be people in  ukraine who appreciate that and are  grateful for that so i i i try not to  have too too strong an opinion on it i  think if if people feel that that  somehow signals something to others  great i try to  i always try to think about taking  actions that help uh rather than  uh signaling things that that make me  feel good again  which you said you you had your  fundraiser you raised fifty thousand  fifty five thousand pounds with your um  uh your co-host uh uh francis and uh can  you tell us a little bit about uh  if people want to donate more  are we still able to do that through you  uh for you guys uh and where's that  money going uh so we picked three  charities one is a polish charity that's  working on the ground uh in poland and a  couple are  uh british and american charities that  do very specific targeted medical uh and  uh mental health support for people who  are fleeing war uh the names of all  three escape me now but um  there are lots of charities doing great  work the british cross uh red not the  british the red cross uh ukraine appeal  and many many others so uh people can  just donate directly to those if you  just google you know reliable charities  ukraine there's plenty to donate to and  these are charities like i say that are  helping people on the ground in the  countries around so um that's to me  really what i would encourage people to  do  uh and all of this talk and signaling  whatever look it's not it doesn't do 